Prerequisites
1. A valid GitHub account, registered and logged in before you begin.
2. A stable Internet connection.
3. A web browser such as Chrome, Edge, or Firefox.
Steps
1. Go to https://github.com/ and sign in with your username and password.
2. Click the “+” icon in the top-right corner and select “New repository”.
3. Enter a repository name, choose whether it will be public or private, and select “Add a README file”.
4. Click “Create repository” to finish setting up the project.
5. Open the README file from your new repository and click the pencil icon to edit it.
Result Check
1. You can see your repository name listed on your GitHub profile.
2. The README.md file is present in the repository and editable.
3. The repository page displays correctly without loading errors.
